    "created_at": "2016-06-09T12:27:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-09T12:27:42Z",
    "body": "> Maybe say that [NamedConstructor] is fair game?\n\nYeah, good idea.\n\n> Why did you go for explicitly annotating all subclasses rather than letting them inherit the annotation?\n\nYou can do that? It seems like it would be weird action-at-a-distance, but if there's precedent for other extended attributes, I guess maybe it's OK...\n\n> There's a bit of an open question in my mind about whether super(100, 100) will work when you're extending 'img' or super('hello', true, true) is allowable if you're extending 'option', that sort of thing. But I am pretty confident we can make anything work, within reason.\n\nHmm. So `Option !== HTMLOptionElement`, so e.g. doing `class X extends HTMLOptionElement { constructor() { super('hello', true, true); } }` will not work. But maybe `class X extends Option { constructor() { super('hello', true, true); } }` would work... I can't immediately think of any reason why it would not. I will think it through more.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
