      "site_admin": false
    },
    "created_at": "2016-06-10T09:05:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-10T09:05:44Z",
    "body": "> We shouldn't allow people to inherit from HTMLUnknownElement since no native elements do, and they never will. The whole point of being an unknown element is that you're unknown, not defined...\n\nExcept when we add a new element, it changes from unknown to defined, and for some period of time it will be unknown in some UAs and defined in other UAs. In such a situation people will want to polyfill the element for browsers that don't yet support it natively (c.f. `picture`).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
