    "updated_at": "2016-06-10T15:23:03Z",
    "body": "> Except when we add a new element, it changes from unknown to defined, and for some period of time it will be unknown in some UAs and defined in other UAs. In such a situation people will want to polyfill the element for browsers that don't yet support it natively (c.f. picture).\n\nYes, sure. But they won't do it by inheriting from HTMLUnknownElement when creating their custom element. That still wouldn't make any sense.\n",
