    "created_at": "2016-06-10T22:22:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-10T22:22:19Z",
    "body": "> That seems a lot more straightforward than having to carefully annotate everything except for that.\n\nI don't think that's true. I think it's more straightforward to say that the [HTMLConstructor] annotation is like the [Constructor] annotation: both of them say \"this interface has constructor behavior, so when generating the bindings code for this interface, be sure to generate a constructor.\" [HTMLConstructor] simply says that the algorithm is a specific algorithm, not defined in interface-specific prose. But in both cases, it's a per-interface property, and IMO we should avoid the action at a distance.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
